---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout title="Scaling a Lean Sourcing Team Without Adding Headcount - Marker">
  <Navbar />
  <main id="main-content">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-16 md:pt-24 md:pb-24">
      <a
        href="/case-studies"
        class="mb-8 inline-flex items-center text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground"
      >
        <svg
          class="mr-1 h-4 w-4"
          fill="none"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
        >
          <path
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path>
        </svg>
        All Case Studies
      </a>

      <span
        class="mb-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-primary"
      >
        Outdoor Apparel
      </span>
      <h1
        class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl"
      >
        Scaling a Lean Sourcing Team Without Adding Headcount
      </h1>

      <div
        class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/50 p-5 text-sm"
      >
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Company</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground"
              >Sustainability-focused outdoor apparel brand</span
            >
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Team</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground"
              >Small sourcing team managing a 12-18 month product cycle</span
            >
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Key Challenge</span
            >
            <span class="text-muted-foreground"
              >Communication scattered across email, WhatsApp, and Slack with no
              way to prioritize what needs attention</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Challenge</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          A senior sourcing leader at this outdoor apparel brand — with
          experience across multiple major retailers — was managing a team that
          received 80 or more emails daily, on top of messages coming in through
          WhatsApp and Slack. The volume made it impossible to read and
          comprehend everything. Critical messages were getting buried alongside
          routine updates.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          The team had evaluated nine different software products and onboarded
          none of them. The sourcing leader noted that most tools were "being
          built with basics in mind" and didn't account for the complexity of
          fashion sourcing, where styles change every season and bills of
          materials can have dozens of sub-components. She also observed that
          "nine out of ten" software vendors pitching to her team had "never set
          foot in a factory."
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          Meanwhile, the industry trend was clear: "The days of big teams are
          gone." The brand needed to increase sourcing output — expanding into
          new countries of origin and managing more complex supply chains — with
          the same headcount.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Approach</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          Marker integrates with the team's existing communication channels —
          email, WhatsApp, and Slack — without asking anyone to change how they
          work. Instead of requiring the team to adopt a new portal, Marker
          captures the communication stream where it already happens and
          organizes it around the product calendar.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          The key capability for this team was intelligent bucketing: separating
          messages that need the sourcing leader's attention from routine updates
          that can be handled by the broader team or deferred. Rather than
          scanning 80 emails for the five that matter, the team starts their day
          with a prioritized view of what requires action.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
          Marker also layers a calendar overlay onto communications, connecting
          supplier messages to sourcing strategy milestones. When a deadline is
          approaching and communication has gone quiet — or when a supplier
          response pattern suggests a delay is likely — the team is alerted. This
          gives the small team the situational awareness that previously required
          either more people or more hours.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">Key Takeaways</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-muted-foreground">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >Communication from email, WhatsApp, and Slack captured in one
              place without changing how the team works</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >Intelligent prioritization separates messages that need senior
              attention from routine updates</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >Calendar overlay connects supplier messages to sourcing strategy
              milestones and flags risks</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >No new portal adoption required — integrates into existing
              communication channels</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"
            ></span>
            <span
              >Enables a small team to manage growing complexity across
              countries of origin and supplier relationships</span
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section
        class="mt-12 rounded-lg border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 p-6 text-center"
      >
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-foreground">
          See how Marker helps lean teams do more without adding headcount.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/book-demo"
          class="mt-4 inline-flex h-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary px-6 text-sm font-medium text-primary-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-primary/90 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2"
        >
          Book a Demo
        </a>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
